# v1 improved: order from the simulator's search (Human Alliance, 2000000 tries, seeded with v1's order;
# 125.7 h -> 117.5 h to 60 in the model), written by polestar apply-route.
# Added here: Look to the Stars (181), The Weathered Grave (225), The Thandol Span (632), Sully Balloo's Letter (637), MacKreel's Moonshine (647).
# 5 goals moved in from other guides of the chain.
# The notes above describe v1's order; the steps below are the improved one.

# Duskwood, the Wetlands and the Shimmering Flats, Alliance ~28.2 to ~30.4.
#
# Route from the simulator's consensus Alliance route (Human export, visits
# 11-13: Duskwood 28.2-29.1, Wetlands 29.1-29.6, Thousand Needles
# 29.6-30.4), written out as a playable guide; not play-tested on Forever
# yet.
#
# Flow: fly Stormwind -> Darkshire (hearth) -> the worgen
# of Brightwood and the south, Blind Mary and the Insane Ghoul -> Darkshire
# -> west: Abercrombie, the Plague Spreaders, Sven and the Raven Hill
# Cemetery, the Defias strongbox, the Vul'Gol crate, Abercrombie -> hearth to
# Darkshire -> fly to Menethil Harbor (hearth) -> the Third Fleet's wreck,
# the Bluegill Raiders and the north coast -> Menethil -> the wreck ->
# Menethil -> east: the dig, Sarltooth, the Dragonmaw ->
# Menethil -> the Angerfang Encampment's attack plans -> hearth -> Menethil
# -> boat to Theramore -> the
# Great Lift -> the Shimmering Flats -> hearth to Menethil, where
# 30-40/01-hillsbrad-foothills picks up (the Forever Wetlands quests, then
# the boat to Southshore).
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Look To The Stars (174-177) is turned in on arrival in Darkshire instead
#   of at the end of the visit: Viktori stands on the way, and the Insane
#   Ghoul sits beside the worgen of the south.
# - Apprentice's Duties (471, accepted in the previous guide) is finished on
#   the north coast beside the wreck and turned in here.
# - Henrig Lonebrow's Journal (1100) is picked up at the foot of the Great
#   Lift on the way in (the export takes it at the end of the visit).
# - All Mirage Raceway quests are taken on the first visit; one loop of the
#   flats finishes them all.
# - The Legend of Stalvan (67) is not taken: the export never turns it in
#   (the Old Footlocker is in Westfall).
# - Refresh (2026): Merrick's Bow (96138, Forever, in the new consensus)
#   is optional at the Vul'Gol mound: it starts from Merrick's Bow, which
#   the Lost Watchers of Duskwood drop (rate unknown), asks for 8 Splinter
#   Fist Warriors and 4 Taskmasters and ends at Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.
# - Refresh: the guide ends on the hearth to Menethil Harbor; the Southshore
#   boat, flight path, bind and The Shamed Lieutenant (98219) moved to
#   30-40/01-hillsbrad-foothills, which first runs the Forever Wetlands
#   quests of the new consensus's 30-31 visit. The new consensus visits
#   Thousand Needles later (32.6, after Hillsbrad); the Shimmering Flats stay
#   here, between the Wetlands and the hearth, as before.
# - Mirage Raceway: Zherin and Pozzik, first on the way in from the salt
#   flats, before Fizzle, Wizzle and Kravel.
# - Forever puts From the Ashes (98221) between War Banners (464) and
#   Nek'rosh's Gambit (465): Captain Stoutfist offers 465 only once 98221 is
#   handed in (issue #225, Lou-Saydus, in game). 98221 is taken when the
#   banners are handed in and done on the trip east that used to light the
#   catapult; 465 is taken when it is handed in after the hearth, and the
#   catapult is lit on the Wetlands loop of 30-40/01-hillsbrad-foothills.
#   The Attack Plans are not in the data: the step points at the camp's
#   Tattered Spellbook (671518), the spot the data has inside the camp.
#
# Dropped for flow: A Noble Brew (335, 2450 XP): the Musquash Root sits in
# the far south-east of the Wetlands, a long detour off the route, and the
# Tear of Tilloa another one north of Darkshire. Not accepted in Stormwind
# (06-ashenvale) either; no grind needed for under a tenth of a level.
#
# Class quests: Warlocks hand Devourer of Souls (1716, from Stormwind in
# 04-redridge-mountains) to Takar the Seer on the ride through the Barrens and
# take Heartswood (1738); the Heartswood is in Ashenvale (30-40/02-desolace).
# Warlocks may also take What Is Love? (65602, the incubus) from Takar;
# optional, finished in 30-40/02-desolace and 30-40/05-arathi-highlands
# (forever/class/warlock/incubus-alliance has the whole chain).
#
# Left out (not in the export): Bride of the Embalmer (253: elites), The
# Weathered Grave (225: elite Mor'Ladim), Defeat Nek'rosh (474: elite).
# Checked and skipped: The Scythe of Elune (1043) needs The Carevin Family
# (1041, 1042), a chain from Darkshore and Ashenvale the route never starts.
# Keeping Pace and Rizzle's Schematics (1190, 1194) need News for Fizzle
# (1137), which comes after Martek in the Badlands at 38.

